# Testing and Quality

- Map tests to FR/BR or story AC IDs — not to informal chat.
- Write `docs/test-cases.md` (case bodies with full steps + expected) **and** `docs/test-matrix.md` (index). **br-coverage-validator** (quality-agent) is the only writer of `docs/test-cases-br-coverage.md`. Implementers must not stamp PASS. The matrix is not a substitute for case bodies.
- Classify BR Type with `.cursor/templates/br-tc-taxonomy.md` before authoring negatives. Zero generic step placeholders (`.cursor/templates/generic-step-denylist.md`). Completeness + step-quality validators must PASS on expand. Heuristic bulk generators are forbidden. Do **not** generate or refresh `docs/test/manual/**` on default expand.
- **PASS + human Approved** (`docs/quality/test-package-review.md`) required before `/run-tests` script generation or execution. FAIL → stay in expand; do not request approval. Silence on coverage gate file = FAIL for expand Done.
- Slice tests on implement-*, fix-issue (defect and cited-requirements), generate-python-module, and validate-api-endpoints still require coverage PASS before **that slice’s** scripts. Expand coverage PASS does **not** block implement-api/implement-ui (**ASSUMPTION-PCC-002** — see `.cursor/docs/factory-assumptions.md` and `docs/harness/decisions.md`).
- When an integration test writes shared vault, summary, or xref rows, include an idempotent `@BeforeEach` restore of those rows. This is part of the existing IT update on `/implement-api`. Do not add a pipeline stage.
- New screen unit tests must use the UI module’s existing themed render helper (`renderAudit` only if that export already exists). Record a missing helper as infra debt in the expand audit. Do not add a test stage.
- Line coverage floor from `config.yaml` `quality_gates.api_unit_line_coverage_min`.
- Positive and mandatory negative API cases (taxonomy: Constraint and Condition-gate).
- Quality-agent and eval-agent MUST NOT lower gates or disable JaCoCo/coverage checks. Quality-agent must not waive companion step-quality.
- Eval-agent runs only via `/run-eval`. It must emit a completeness ledger. Silence (no case, skipped always-on safety family, skipped agent-result check) is a finding, not a pass. Incremental evals still include L1-04, L1-05, L1-08, L1-09, L4-03. Cannot waive P0/P1.
- `/review-changes` requires a `/run-eval` completeness ledger; do not run eval-agent inside review.
- Untrusted intake (Figma, Excel, CSV) must pass `scripts/intake-safety-scan.py` before case authoring. Trusted BRD/stories/OpenAPI skip scan.
- CODEOWNERS (or equivalent) must protect gate files (`pom.xml`, CI workflows).
